{"text": "PAYROLL SUMMARY\nPrairie Rose Bakery & Cafe LLC | EIN 45-3381072 | ND withholding acct\nWTH-2209417\n\nPay period 20: 10/16/2026 to 10/31/2026. Check date 11/05/2026. Processed by Red\nRiver Payroll Partners, batch RR-118820.\n\nEmployee totals\nEmployee ID Gross Net\nNguyen, Bao E-1003 $2,480.00 $1,902.44\nWindsong, April E-1007 $1,612.50 $1,288.07\nWisniewski, T. E-1011 $1,944.00 $1,067.91\nRobinson, Deja E-1015 $386.25 $342.18\nHernandez, G. E-1016 $1,530.00 $1,241.60\nTotal $7,952.75 $5,842.20\n\nNotes for the owner\nIngrid Solberg asked for plain-language notes this cycle, so here they are.\n\nBao Nguyen (head baker) had 6.5 hours of overtime. His direct deposit changed\nthis period to Dakota Plains Credit Union, routing 022797346, account 7002 118\n4460. He brought the form in himself.\n\nApril is back from maternity leave as of the 19th, part time. Her Form W-4\nchanged; she now has two dependents.\n\nTomasz Wisniewski's net is low. There is a child support order that takes $412.00\nper period (the case number is 08-2023-DM-00417), plus UFCW Local 1161 dues of\n$18.50 (he is the only union member on staff, carried over from his grocery job\nunder the transfer card). The state unit asked us to confirm his SSN, which is\n433622202 in our records.\n\nDeja Robinson is a minor (DOB 06/30/2010), hours capped on school days. Her\nwork permit is on file. Her father, Malik Robinson, asked that her pay go to a\ncustodial account; we need a voided check first.\n\nGuadalupe Hernandez Ortiz started 10/19/2026. Her I-9 was completed with a\npermanent resident card, number A-208-417-339. Please keep the copy out of the\ngeneral personnel folder.\n\nEmployer taxes this period\nFICA match $608.39. FUTA $11.20. State unemployment $87.48. The 401(k) match\nis 0.00 because nobody is enrolled yet. The Form 941 deposit of $1,811.06 drafts on\nthe check date.\n\nQuestions to payroll@redriverpayroll.example or 701-555-0166.", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 298 words",